&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a senior IT engineer to own Qventus&#39; IT infrastructure. This role will be responsible for integrating IT, Engineering, and HR systems; keeping our IAM group design coherent; and working cross-team to streamline IT processes by building a strong foundation for automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer and integrate IT systems so that they &quot;just work&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate the manual IT work so that provisioning is repeatable, access is right-sized, and lifecycle runs itself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Know what we run and who can reach it, and keep that picture authoritative as the company changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own our endpoint management system and policy implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Security and DevOps so the foundation is a source of leverage others build on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive complex, ambiguous projects forward independently, set priorities across disparate systems, and communicate tradeoffs clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with identity and access management in SaaS-heavy environments, including SCIM provisioning and HR-driven lifecycle automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in owning systems that handle PHI, in a HIPAA-regulated or similarly regulated environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on endpoint management engineering experience with tools like NinjaOne&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort treating infrastructure as code and building maintainable tooling in a language like Python or Go&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SaaS administration, OAuth-grant and access governance, and maintaining an authoritative application inventory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
